SQL Query Sample (Book Category Insight Post-2010)
This example illustrates the retrieval of book categories containing at least one book published after 2010. It highlights total books, available copies, and distinct publisher counts:

SELECT
    c.category_name,
    COUNT(b.book_id) AS total_books,
    SUM(b.copies_available) AS total_copies_available,
    COUNT(DISTINCT b.publisher_id) AS distinct_publishers_count
FROM tbl_category c
JOIN tbl_book b ON c.category_id = b.category_id
WHERE YEAR(b.publication_year) > 2010
GROUP BY c.category_id, c.category_name
ORDER BY total_books DESC, category_name;
Explanation: This query succinctly links categories to books and checks for post-2010 publications, aggregates book numbers, available copies, and publisher diversity .
Practical Tips
Use LEFT JOIN when you need all records from one table, regardless of match status in another.
Handle NULL values with caution, particularly when counting.
Strategic use of UNION and UNION ALL helps combine multiple datasets with different filter criteria without duplication issues .
